<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Deliberately empty.

	The Live Activity appex draws a session count and some tab titles that
	ActivityKit hands it. It opens nothing, spawns nothing, and talks to
	nothing: no mach-lookup exception, and above all no
	wiki.qaq.ighostvt.client — the daemon must never accept a connection from
	anything but the app binary itself, and package-deb.sh fails the build if
	this file ever grows either key.

	A standard sandboxed extension is exactly what this needs to be, so there
	is nothing to ask for. `ldid` still needs the file: signing with an empty
	entitlement set is the statement, not the absence of one.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
